# The ISO build needs the scripts that assemble the boot tree, and nothing
# else. The repository and the signing key both arrive as named build contexts
# (ductrepo, ductkey): the repository because it is hundreds of megabytes and
# changes on every package build, and the key because which one is correct
# depends on which repository is being installed from.
#
# Deny-everything allowlist: a new COPY in the Dockerfile needs a line here or
# it fails with "file not found in build context", which reads as a missing
# file rather than an excluded one.
*
!images/iso/
!images/scripts/seed-etc.sh

**/.git/
**/.DS_Store
